WEBVTT

00:00.468 --> 00:02.688
== Sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00ff00">elderman&lt;/font> ==
== for &lt;font color=00FFFF>www.addic7ed.com&lt;/font> ==
♪ Men. ♪

00:02.778 --> 00:05.780
All right, I have
turned "it" into "ziti,"

00:05.781 --> 00:09.550
Uh, with a triple letter on z
and a double word on the I.

00:09.551 --> 00:13.387
Plus, going down,
I've created "za."

00:15.113 --> 00:15.699
Za?

00:15.899 --> 00:17.830
Uh, a colloquialism for pizza.

00:18.736 --> 00:20.186
One of the five
two-letter words

00:20.187 --> 00:22.555
newly accepted by the National
Scrabble Association.

00:22.556 --> 00:25.375
Unbelievable.

00:25.376 --> 00:27.443
You can call them
if you want.

00:28.946 --> 00:30.813
That's what we
in Scrabble circles call

00:30.814 --> 00:32.115
a two tile takedown.

00:32.116 --> 00:34.117
♪ Bom-bom! ♪

00:34.118 --> 00:36.018
CHARLIE:
Hey, Alan,

00:36.019 --> 00:37.370
is our limo here yet?

00:37.371 --> 00:39.155
Uh, sorry,
I haven't seen a limo.

00:39.156 --> 00:40.239
Oh, 100 points!

00:40.240 --> 00:41.574
♪ Bow-bow! ♪

00:42.426 --> 00:44.861
That's a gorgeous dress,
Courtney.

00:44.862 --> 00:46.379
Thanks. Charlie
insisted on buying it

00:46.380 --> 00:47.630
for me to wear
tonight.

00:47.631 --> 00:48.798
What's the
charity again?

00:48.799 --> 00:50.800
I don't know.
Landmines, orphans.

00:50.801 --> 00:52.869
Landmines for orphans.

00:52.870 --> 00:54.303
I just want
to show you off.

00:54.304 --> 00:55.271
Oh.

00:55.272 --> 00:56.706
Well, you look great.

00:56.707 --> 00:57.673
Thank you.

00:57.674 --> 00:59.509
No, no.
No, there's...

00:59.510 --> 01:02.061
something...
something wrong.

01:02.062 --> 01:03.446
What?

01:03.447 --> 01:04.847
I don't know. I don't know.

01:04.848 --> 01:06.549
Something's...
something's missing.

01:06.550 --> 01:09.102
Oh, I got it.

01:09.103 --> 01:10.853
Ta-dah!

01:10.854 --> 01:12.021
Charlie!

01:12.022 --> 01:13.356
(gasps)

01:13.357 --> 01:15.074
You shouldn't have.

01:15.075 --> 01:17.443
Well, you've done a
lot of things for me

01:17.444 --> 01:19.729
&lt;i>you&lt;/i> shouldn't have.

01:21.365 --> 01:23.082
Oh, my...
&lt;i>Now&lt;/i> you look great.

01:23.083 --> 01:24.917
God, it is beautiful.

01:24.918 --> 01:27.170
Thank you.

01:38.115 --> 01:40.683
So, what are you
guys up to tonight?

01:40.684 --> 01:43.820
Oh, not much. Just a quiet,
romantic evening at home.

01:43.821 --> 01:45.421
Loser.

01:46.990 --> 01:48.925
Come on, that's not fair.

01:48.926 --> 01:51.760
No, it's my
word-- loser.

01:51.761 --> 01:54.230
Oh. Oh. Oh, uh, well,
then I should point out

01:54.231 --> 01:55.898
that you could have used the C

01:55.899 --> 01:58.284
at the top of the board
and made "closer."

01:59.136 --> 02:01.337
I'll stick with loser.

02:01.338 --> 02:03.706
(phone ringing)

02:03.707 --> 02:05.491
Yeah?

02:05.492 --> 02:07.510
Great. We'll be right out.

02:07.511 --> 02:08.945
Our chariot awaits.

02:08.946 --> 02:09.912
Have fun.

02:09.913 --> 02:11.080
Thanks. You, too.

02:11.081 --> 02:12.248
Do me a favor.

02:12.249 --> 02:13.649
When we get in the limo,

02:13.650 --> 02:15.585
ask the driver
to put up the partition.

02:15.586 --> 02:16.719
You bet.

02:16.720 --> 02:18.020
Isn't that sweet?

02:18.021 --> 02:20.173
She's gonna do more things
she shouldn't.

02:27.514 --> 02:29.732
Gluten-free pretzel?

02:29.733 --> 02:31.467
No, thanks.

02:31.468 --> 02:34.687
Oh, I guess this isn't much
of a Saturday night date.

02:34.688 --> 02:36.172
Alan, it's fine.

02:36.173 --> 02:37.740
I like staying
in with you.

02:37.741 --> 02:41.310
I could probably do
without the ♪ Bom-bom! ♪

02:41.311 --> 02:43.946
Well, I just... I wish
I could take you out

02:43.947 --> 02:46.365
and get you things
like Charlie does.

02:46.366 --> 02:48.317
I don't need those things.

02:48.318 --> 02:50.653
I mean, they're nice.

02:50.654 --> 02:52.021
They're more than nice.

02:52.022 --> 02:53.656
They're what every
girl dreams of.

02:53.657 --> 02:55.458
But let's face it.

02:55.459 --> 02:58.227
Some dreams just
have to die.

02:59.730 --> 03:02.398
Well, I'm-I'm sorry
you had to settle.

03:02.399 --> 03:04.383
I'm not settling.

03:04.384 --> 03:06.135
I'm... I'm accepting.

03:06.136 --> 03:08.337
So you're not rich and
successful like Charlie.

03:08.338 --> 03:10.506
So you can't take
me out in limos

03:10.507 --> 03:11.891
and shower me in diamonds.

03:11.892 --> 03:13.442
So there's no
expensive restaurants

03:13.443 --> 03:15.177
or beautiful dresses.

03:20.617 --> 03:22.585
But?

03:22.586 --> 03:24.086
What?

03:24.087 --> 03:26.205
Well, you know,
I can't take you out,

03:26.206 --> 03:29.792
and I can't give
you stuff, but...

03:29.793 --> 03:32.929
But... I love you?

03:32.930 --> 03:35.398
Why?

03:36.633 --> 03:39.802
Boy, you're just gonna keep
pushing this, aren't you?

03:39.803 --> 03:41.971
No, no. You love me. I'm good.

03:41.972 --> 03:43.306
Let's play Scrabble.

03:43.307 --> 03:44.473
Mm.

03:44.474 --> 03:45.841
Ooh, axolotl!

03:45.842 --> 03:48.010
(laughs)

03:49.212 --> 03:50.563
Uh...

03:50.564 --> 03:52.481
(quietly):
♪ Bom-bom. ♪

03:52.482 --> 03:55.151
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

03:55.152 --> 03:56.475
♪ Oh-oh. ♪
♪ Men. ♪
♪ Men. ♪

03:56.675 --> 03:59.775
&lt;font color="#00ff00">♪ Two and a Half Men 8x11 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00ffff">Dead From the Waist Down&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on December 6, 2010

03:59.840 --> 04:01.807
♪ Men. ♪

04:02.628 --> 04:03.912
Morning.

04:03.913 --> 04:06.080
Morning.

04:07.066 --> 04:09.934
Pottery Barn?

04:09.935 --> 04:11.553
Yeah, I'm looking for ideas

04:11.554 --> 04:13.404
for a birthday present
for Lyndsey.

04:13.405 --> 04:15.540
At the Pottery Barn?

04:15.541 --> 04:17.408
Well, I don't have your money.

04:17.409 --> 04:19.511
And there are ways
to communicate your feelings

04:19.512 --> 04:21.679
for a woman besides
throwing diamonds at her.

04:21.680 --> 04:24.382
True, but diamonds get you
limo skull.

04:26.185 --> 04:27.735
Pottery Barn won't get you
dry humped

04:27.736 --> 04:29.254
in the back of a city bus.

04:29.255 --> 04:31.756
Charming.

04:31.757 --> 04:34.259
So, uh, how was
the charity soirée last night?

04:34.260 --> 04:37.328
I don't know. We never
made it out of the limo.

04:37.329 --> 04:39.731
Charlie, do you have any idea
how bad you're making me look?

04:39.732 --> 04:41.432
Oh, buddy, that's not me.

04:41.433 --> 04:43.635
That's genetics
and barber school haircuts.

04:43.636 --> 04:45.870
I'm serious. How do you think
it makes me feel

04:45.871 --> 04:48.122
when I'm with Lyndsey,
and I have to watch you

04:48.123 --> 04:49.507
shower Courtney
with limos and diamonds?

04:49.508 --> 04:50.909
Huh. I never thought about that.

04:50.910 --> 04:52.310
I do have a solution, though.

04:52.311 --> 04:54.712
What's that?
Move out.

04:54.713 --> 04:56.481
I-I'm just saying,

04:56.482 --> 04:58.099
I'd appreciate it
if you didn't do so much

04:58.100 --> 04:59.184
of that stuff in front of us.

04:59.185 --> 05:00.852
Again, I have
a solution.

05:00.853 --> 05:02.554
All right, all right, let's just
stipulate for the record

05:02.555 --> 05:04.822
that you want me to move out and
I'm not going anywhere, okay?

05:04.823 --> 05:06.274
What is it you'd have me do?

05:06.275 --> 05:07.609
Not enjoy the money that I earn?

05:07.610 --> 05:09.427
Not lavish it
on the people that I love?

05:09.428 --> 05:11.396
Sneak around in the middle
of the night giving gifts

05:11.397 --> 05:13.331
to my girlfriend, so you don't
get your feelings hurt?

05:13.332 --> 05:15.867
Is that something
you'd consider?

05:15.868 --> 05:19.470
No, but I'll tell you what I will do.
Oh, what's that?

05:19.471 --> 05:21.105
If I should come home some night

05:21.106 --> 05:24.275
to find you standing on a chair
with a rope around your neck

05:24.276 --> 05:25.777
because you can't bear
another moment

05:25.778 --> 05:26.878
of your pathetic life,

05:26.879 --> 05:29.514
I give you my word,
I will kick the chair.

05:33.002 --> 05:35.320
Ooh! Santa Claus bottle stopper.

05:35.321 --> 05:37.322
Only 12 dollars.

05:37.323 --> 05:40.291
I can get her two.

05:40.292 --> 05:42.827
♪ Men. ♪

05:42.828 --> 05:44.495
Dad?

05:44.496 --> 05:46.681
Yeah?

05:47.499 --> 05:49.167
I need money.

05:49.168 --> 05:51.069
Join the club.

05:51.070 --> 05:53.771
Seriously. My clothes
are getting too small.

05:53.772 --> 05:55.990
Jake, I give your mother money
every month

05:55.991 --> 05:58.776
for the express purpose
of buying you whatever you need.

05:58.777 --> 06:00.912
Yeah, well,
that's not how she sees it.

06:00.913 --> 06:02.980
I don't know what
to tell you, buddy.

06:02.981 --> 06:04.916
Things are a little tight
right now.

06:04.917 --> 06:06.551
So are my shoes.

06:06.552 --> 06:09.621
What do you want me to do,
tap into your college fund?

06:09.622 --> 06:12.040
I guess not.

06:12.041 --> 06:14.158
Hang on a second.

06:15.327 --> 06:17.512
Let's not throw that idea out
so quickly.

06:17.513 --> 06:18.730
What do you mean?

06:18.731 --> 06:20.665
Well, realistically,

06:20.666 --> 06:23.935
do you actually see yourself
going to college?

06:23.936 --> 06:25.336
Because if you don't,

06:25.337 --> 06:28.022
we could use that money
to buy you some new clothes,

06:28.023 --> 06:30.441
plus maybe some other things.

06:30.442 --> 06:32.076
You know, it's funny
that you ask that.

06:32.077 --> 06:34.412
I had no interest in college
until a few days ago.

06:34.413 --> 06:35.947
What changed?

06:35.948 --> 06:38.916
I saw this video called
&lt;i>Topless Coeds of the Big Ten,&lt;/i>

06:38.917 --> 06:41.352
and I decided
I need to go to college.

06:41.353 --> 06:44.956
You expect me
to pay 30, 40,000 dollars a year

06:44.957 --> 06:47.592
so you can meet drunk girls
who lift their shirts?

06:47.593 --> 06:49.727
Yes, please.

06:49.728 --> 06:52.130
(grunts)

06:52.131 --> 06:53.898
Is that a no
on the clothes money?

06:53.899 --> 06:56.134
I'll talk
to your mother about it.

06:56.135 --> 06:58.803
Oh, now I'm filled
with hope.

06:58.804 --> 07:01.372
CHARLIE:
Hey, Alan,
come here.

07:01.373 --> 07:04.676
Are you gonna
make me feel worse?

07:04.677 --> 07:06.544
Is that even
possible?

07:06.545 --> 07:09.814
I wouldn't think so, but
you usually find a way.

07:09.815 --> 07:12.250
What do you want?

07:12.251 --> 07:14.252
Well, I couldn't help
but overhear you trying

07:14.253 --> 07:16.254
to talk Huckleberry out
of getting an education.

07:16.255 --> 07:17.905
Yeah, not my proudest moment.

07:17.906 --> 07:19.691
But I'm desperate to find a way

07:19.692 --> 07:21.492
to buy Lyndsey a decent
birthday present.

07:21.493 --> 07:23.461
All right,
here's what I'm gonna do.

07:23.462 --> 07:26.431
I'm gonna "lend" you enough so
you can buy her something nice.

07:26.432 --> 07:27.832
How much are we talking about?

07:27.833 --> 07:29.000
Are you kidding?

07:29.001 --> 07:30.234
You're negotiating with me?!

07:30.235 --> 07:31.902
No, no, forget it.

07:31.903 --> 07:34.772
I appreciate the offer, but
I'm not gonna take your money.

07:34.773 --> 07:37.592
I'm-I'm sorry. I think I might
have just had a small stroke.

07:37.593 --> 07:40.445
I thought I heard you say
you're not gonna take my money.

07:40.446 --> 07:41.612
Yeah, you heard me right.

07:41.613 --> 07:42.964
I have to find a way

07:42.965 --> 07:45.183
to buy Lyndsey a nice present
on my own.

07:45.184 --> 07:46.384
It's a matter of self-respect.

07:46.385 --> 07:48.186
Little late for that, isn't it?

07:48.187 --> 07:49.854
If it was for me,
I'd take your money.

07:49.855 --> 07:52.156
If it was for you,
I wouldn't offer it.

07:52.157 --> 07:53.825
But this is my girlfriend.

07:53.826 --> 07:56.144
If I can't do this one thing
for her,

07:56.145 --> 07:58.196
then maybe
I just don't deserve her.

07:58.197 --> 07:59.997
Okay, what's your plan?

07:59.998 --> 08:01.466
I'm not sure,

08:01.467 --> 08:04.101
but when Alan Harper sets
his mind to something,

08:04.102 --> 08:07.004
just stand back
and watch it happen.

08:07.005 --> 08:08.539
Yeah, right.

08:08.540 --> 08:10.775
Cue the theme from &lt;i>Rocky.&lt;/i>

08:11.777 --> 08:14.278
(Instrumental intro
for &lt;i>Gonna Fly Now&lt;/i> plays)

08:43.642 --> 08:45.910
♪ ♪

09:01.794 --> 09:07.181
♪ Trying hard now ♪

09:07.182 --> 09:12.437
♪ It's so hard now ♪

09:12.438 --> 09:16.741
♪ Trying hard now... ♪

09:46.305 --> 09:48.556
♪ ♪

09:56.615 --> 10:01.452
♪ Getting strong now ♪

10:01.453 --> 10:05.523
♪ Won't be long now ♪

10:05.524 --> 10:08.392
♪ Getting strong now... ♪

10:08.393 --> 10:11.696
(Charlie playing
&lt;i>Rocky&lt;/i> theme song on piano)

10:17.402 --> 10:18.636
(song ends)

10:18.637 --> 10:20.788
(Alan grumbling)

10:24.977 --> 10:26.944
Need some help?

10:26.945 --> 10:30.081
A little late to ask,
don't you think?

10:30.082 --> 10:31.115
Nope.

10:31.116 --> 10:32.283
(sighs)

10:32.284 --> 10:34.418
Well, the good news is,

10:34.419 --> 10:36.454
I am done.

10:36.455 --> 10:38.422
I have accomplished my mission.

10:38.423 --> 10:40.291
After three weeks
of 16-hour days

10:40.292 --> 10:41.826
at the office and the mall,

10:41.827 --> 10:43.594
I have managed
to earn enough money

10:43.595 --> 10:45.897
to buy Lyndsey
a beautiful birthday present.

10:45.898 --> 10:47.365
Voilà!

10:47.366 --> 10:52.937
A matching set of natural
South Sea Island pearls.

10:52.938 --> 10:54.238
No kidding?

10:54.239 --> 10:55.473
Mm-hmm.

10:55.474 --> 10:57.375
And you got these at the mall?

10:57.376 --> 10:58.943
Uh, well, in the
mall parking lot.

10:58.944 --> 11:02.213
Oh, Alan, you bought pearls
from a guy in a parking lot?

11:02.214 --> 11:03.648
(groans) Not a &lt;i>guy.&lt;/i>

11:03.649 --> 11:05.917
A Tahitian wholesaler.

11:05.918 --> 11:08.386
Do you have any idea what the
mark-up is on these things?

11:08.387 --> 11:10.671
By eliminating the middleman,
I saved a fortune.

11:10.672 --> 11:11.856
You sure about that?

11:11.857 --> 11:13.724
Oh, don't worry,
they're real.

11:13.725 --> 11:17.311
I have a certificate
of authenticity.

11:18.430 --> 11:21.365
The word "authenti""
doesn't have a "K" in it.

11:21.366 --> 11:24.869
It's the man's second
language, Charlie.

11:26.972 --> 11:28.272
All right, but for
future reference,

11:28.273 --> 11:30.541
the way you can tell for
sure if pearls are real

11:30.542 --> 11:31.976
is you rub them
on your teeth.

11:31.977 --> 11:33.110
If they're rough,
they're real,

11:33.111 --> 11:34.195
if they're smooth,
they're fake.

11:34.196 --> 11:36.581
Well, fine, fine--
I will prove it to you.

11:36.582 --> 11:37.999
See?

11:39.334 --> 11:41.285
Mmm, rough.

11:42.220 --> 11:44.755
And... oddly minty.

11:52.664 --> 11:54.699
(crunching)

12:01.373 --> 12:02.506
Oh, darn.

12:02.507 --> 12:04.775
♪ Men... ♪

12:06.086 --> 12:07.637
♪ Men... ♪

12:07.638 --> 12:08.921
Morning.

12:08.922 --> 12:10.590
Morning. Hey, nice pearls.

12:10.591 --> 12:12.642
Found them in the garbage.

12:12.643 --> 12:15.595
Strange some of the things
people throw away.

12:15.596 --> 12:18.631
I also found what looked like
a half-written suicide note

12:18.632 --> 12:20.183
in your brother's
handwriting.

12:20.184 --> 12:21.100
No kidding?

12:21.101 --> 12:22.435
Should I be worried?

12:22.436 --> 12:25.805
You mean that he won't
go through with it?

12:25.806 --> 12:28.374
He'll be fine-- he's just
having some money problems.

12:28.375 --> 12:29.742
Okay. But fair warning--

12:29.743 --> 12:32.612
he offs himself,
I ain't cleaning it up.

12:33.714 --> 12:34.981
Who's offing themselves?

12:34.982 --> 12:35.865
Nobody.

12:35.866 --> 12:37.867
Nobody important.

12:38.985 --> 12:41.287
Hey, I was wondering,
are you going anywhere today?

12:41.288 --> 12:44.023
Don't try to play me,
knucklehead, just ask.

12:44.024 --> 12:45.425
Can I borrow your car?
No.

12:45.426 --> 12:47.760
Come on.
Dude, that's a very expensive car.

12:47.761 --> 12:50.329
There's no way I'm
putting &lt;i>you&lt;/i> behind that wheel.

12:50.330 --> 12:51.547
See you later, Charlie.
I'm going shopping.

12:51.548 --> 12:53.332
Have fun.
JAKE: Courtney,

12:53.333 --> 12:54.701
are you taking
Uncle Charlie's car?

12:54.702 --> 12:56.936
Yeah. Why? I was just thinking
maybe I could drive you.

12:56.937 --> 12:58.738
Save you the hassle
of parking and everything.

12:58.739 --> 13:00.773
Oh, aren't you
the sweetest thing.

13:00.774 --> 13:01.808
Thanks.

13:01.809 --> 13:03.109
See you, handsome!

13:04.278 --> 13:06.479
Yeah, see you, handsome.

13:08.315 --> 13:09.916
Wonderful.

13:09.917 --> 13:13.519
I just got outsmarted
by Mr. Potato Head.

13:14.922 --> 13:16.789
♪ Men... ♪

13:16.790 --> 13:20.059
(football game playing
at low volume)

13:21.095 --> 13:23.262
Hey.
Hey.

13:29.636 --> 13:32.038
I did a bad
thing, Charlie.

13:32.039 --> 13:33.339
Uh-huh.

13:36.276 --> 13:38.277
A &lt;i>very&lt;/i> bad thing.

13:38.278 --> 13:39.679
Sorry to hear it.

13:39.680 --> 13:42.749
I don't even want
to tell you about it.

13:42.750 --> 13:44.884
Good.
I am so ashamed...

13:44.885 --> 13:47.687
Okay, we both know you're gonna
tell me, so just tell me.

13:47.688 --> 13:48.988
Well, in order
to explain it,

13:48.989 --> 13:52.325
I have to go back a few years.
Oh, please, God help me.

13:52.326 --> 13:54.260
Back when Judith and I
were still married

13:54.261 --> 13:55.578
but having problems,
I decided

13:55.579 --> 13:57.897
to try to make her happy
by buying her

13:57.898 --> 14:00.333
a really nice pair
or diamond earrings.

14:00.334 --> 14:01.934
You could afford
diamond earrings?

14:01.935 --> 14:03.736
No alimony,
no child support.

14:03.737 --> 14:05.671
It was a bountiful time.

14:05.672 --> 14:07.206
Uh-huh.
Anyway,

14:07.207 --> 14:10.259
I spent a fortune on them and
I wrapped them up really nice

14:10.260 --> 14:11.844
and took her to
an expensive restaurant

14:11.845 --> 14:13.880
and gave them to her
over cocktails.

14:13.881 --> 14:15.214
And?

14:15.215 --> 14:17.750
She said, "Thanks,"
ordered the lobster,

14:17.751 --> 14:19.719
then filed for divorce.

14:19.720 --> 14:22.421
At which point, I moved in with you.
(sighs)

14:22.422 --> 14:23.489
You're right, Alan,

14:23.490 --> 14:25.825
that &lt;i>was&lt;/i> a
very bad thing.

14:25.826 --> 14:29.228
Oh, no, no, that was just the prologue.
Oh, please, God, help me.

14:29.229 --> 14:31.297
So, this afternoon,
I was over at Judith's

14:31.298 --> 14:33.800
to talk to her about using
my child support payments

14:33.801 --> 14:35.735
to buy Jake new clothes.
Yeah?

14:35.736 --> 14:37.870
She's against it.

14:37.871 --> 14:40.940
We argued, she stormed
out of the room

14:40.941 --> 14:43.476
and left me
standing there by myself

14:43.477 --> 14:45.711
in the house I used to own.

14:45.712 --> 14:48.113
Anyway, before I left,
I figured I'd pee.

14:48.114 --> 14:50.349
I didn't really need
to, but, you know,

14:50.350 --> 14:52.285
you got to figure with the
traffic, it's a good defensiv...

14:52.286 --> 14:53.886
Would you please
get to it!

14:53.887 --> 14:55.054
Al-Almost there,
almost there.

14:55.055 --> 14:57.723
So, as I was walking
down the hallway,

14:57.724 --> 15:01.594
I noticed that Judith's
bedroom door was open,

15:01.595 --> 15:05.298
and... I thought about those
beautiful diamond earrings

15:05.299 --> 15:07.533
just sitting there
in her jewelry box

15:07.534 --> 15:10.503
and how I can't even afford
to buy my girlfriend

15:10.504 --> 15:12.038
a birthday present.

15:12.039 --> 15:13.472
Let me guess.

15:13.473 --> 15:15.708
You peed in her
jewelry box.

15:18.996 --> 15:21.380
Judith never even
wore them, Charlie.

15:21.381 --> 15:24.517
You stole diamonds
from your ex-wife?

15:24.518 --> 15:26.686
Yeah.

15:27.521 --> 15:29.705
Kudos!

15:32.426 --> 15:34.160
I don't even know
how it happened.

15:34.161 --> 15:36.512
I mean, it was
like I was in a dream,

15:36.513 --> 15:38.164
and my hands belonged
to someone else.

15:38.165 --> 15:41.734
I have that same
dream all the time.

15:41.735 --> 15:44.887
Except in mine, the hands
&lt;i>do&lt;/i> belong to someone else.

15:44.888 --> 15:47.356
I-I'm a good man, Charlie;
I play by the rules.

15:47.357 --> 15:48.340
This isn't me.

15:48.341 --> 15:49.909
Sure it is. You
made up your mind

15:49.910 --> 15:51.444
that you were gonna
figure out a way

15:51.445 --> 15:52.895
to get Lyndsey a
nice birthday present.

15:52.896 --> 15:55.081
The only part that isn't
you is that you succeeded.

15:55.082 --> 15:58.251
I can't give these to Lyndsey--
they're tainted.

15:58.252 --> 16:01.571
I have to sneak them back
into Judith's jewelry box.

16:01.572 --> 16:03.923
Aw, you can't do that.
Why not?

16:03.924 --> 16:05.191
Don't you watch TV?

16:05.192 --> 16:07.743
Every time the crooks try
to put the stolen loot back,

16:07.744 --> 16:10.196
it always goes horribly,
and hilariously, wrong.

16:10.197 --> 16:12.298
I will just have
to take that chance.

16:12.299 --> 16:14.033
Tomorrow I am going
back to Judith's,

16:14.034 --> 16:15.468
and I'm gonna make this right.

16:15.469 --> 16:17.270
Suit yourself.

16:17.271 --> 16:19.205
(football game playing
at low volume)

16:19.206 --> 16:21.607
I don't suppose you
want to come with me?

16:21.608 --> 16:24.944
Maybe distract her while
I put the earrings back?

16:24.945 --> 16:26.596
Yeah, that sounds
like a great plan.

16:26.597 --> 16:29.482
What could go wrong?

16:29.483 --> 16:31.250
Okay, I'll
do it myself.

16:31.251 --> 16:33.319
Don't call me
for bail money.

16:33.320 --> 16:35.488
Why not? You were gonna
give me money to buy a present.

16:35.489 --> 16:37.723
You're not even &lt;i>planning&lt;/i>
to get away with it?

16:37.724 --> 16:39.759
Well, of course I am.

16:39.760 --> 16:43.362
I was always &lt;i>planning&lt;/i> to become
an astronaut and a cowboy.

16:46.399 --> 16:48.668
♪ Men... ♪

16:50.370 --> 16:52.271
Hey, baby.
(chuckles): Hey!

16:52.272 --> 16:54.874
How was shopping?
Oh, we had a great time.

16:54.875 --> 16:57.376
Yeah, it was a blast.

16:58.595 --> 17:02.048
Look-- I got the same watch
Johnny Depp has.

17:02.049 --> 17:04.050
Wait, wait, wait,
wait, hold on.

17:04.051 --> 17:05.434
You-you bought him all this?

17:05.435 --> 17:07.019
Well, he was
so helpful.

17:07.020 --> 17:09.055
Here you go, handsome.

17:09.973 --> 17:13.359
Oh, by they way, you
got a parking ticket.

17:17.064 --> 17:18.481
Damn it, Courtney,
I don't want you

17:18.482 --> 17:20.333
buying stuff for that
clown on my credit card.

17:20.334 --> 17:22.335
Why not? You
buy me stuff.

17:22.336 --> 17:23.486
There's a difference.

17:23.487 --> 17:24.453
What's that?

17:24.454 --> 17:26.372
Well, you're having
sex with me,

17:26.373 --> 17:28.791
and he's... well,
he's just screwing me.

17:29.710 --> 17:32.912
(Jake chuckles evilly)

17:34.381 --> 17:36.632
♪ Men... ♪

17:37.584 --> 17:38.834
You okay, honey?

17:38.835 --> 17:40.002
Oh, yeah, yeah.

17:40.003 --> 17:41.587
I'm-I'm just
a little tired.

17:41.588 --> 17:42.788
Oh, of course you are.

17:42.789 --> 17:44.957
You've been working so hard.
Mm-hmm.

17:44.958 --> 17:46.759
I got a little
something for you.

17:46.760 --> 17:50.062
Oh, Lyndsey, not tonight--
I'm dead from the waist down.

17:50.063 --> 17:52.398
Silly! Not that.

17:52.399 --> 17:53.566
This.

17:53.567 --> 17:54.850
Oh. What is it?

17:54.851 --> 17:57.019
Open it and see.

17:58.872 --> 18:02.074
"A day of pampering
at the Beverly Glen Spa"?

18:02.075 --> 18:04.443
You can get a massage,
scalp treatment, facial,

18:04.444 --> 18:05.778
mani-pedi, anything you want.

18:05.779 --> 18:06.912
What's the occasion?

18:06.913 --> 18:09.115
You're my man--
you deserve it.

18:13.553 --> 18:14.920
Oh, boy.

18:14.921 --> 18:16.005
What's the matter?

18:16.006 --> 18:19.091
Well, your birthday's
on Saturday.

18:19.092 --> 18:21.694
Alan... I told you,
I don't expect

18:21.695 --> 18:23.429
anything fancy or expensive.

18:23.430 --> 18:24.997
I know you don't.

18:24.998 --> 18:27.166
(laughs softly)

18:29.036 --> 18:31.637
Which is why I
got you these!

18:32.672 --> 18:33.773
(gasps)

18:33.774 --> 18:36.358
You shouldn't have!

18:36.359 --> 18:38.210
Tell me about it.
(nervous chuckle)

18:38.211 --> 18:40.246
They must have
cost a fortune!

18:40.247 --> 18:41.530
(laughs) Oh, not really.

18:41.531 --> 18:42.782
I stole 'em.

18:42.783 --> 18:45.251
(both laughing)

18:47.154 --> 18:48.988
♪ Men... ♪

18:48.989 --> 18:51.023
Oh. To my
birthday girl.

18:51.024 --> 18:52.708
Thank you, sweetie.

18:52.709 --> 18:56.095
How do they look? Almost as beautiful
as the woman who's wearing them.

18:56.096 --> 18:57.997
Oh, Alan
(laughs)

18:57.998 --> 18:59.598
Hey, hey, hey.

18:59.599 --> 19:01.634
Judith. Judith, Herb.

19:01.635 --> 19:03.719
(laughs)
Um, what a surprise.

19:03.720 --> 19:05.704
What brings &lt;i>you&lt;/i> here?

19:05.705 --> 19:08.407
It's our, uh, weekly
in-lieu-of-sex dinner.

19:08.408 --> 19:10.076
Herb!

19:10.077 --> 19:12.144
Oopsy.

19:12.145 --> 19:14.230
Hi, Lyndsey.
How have you been?

19:14.231 --> 19:15.281
Good, thanks.

19:15.282 --> 19:17.099
Uh, how about you?

19:17.100 --> 19:18.768
Fine.

19:19.770 --> 19:21.420
Alan, what is
wrong with you?

19:21.421 --> 19:22.755
Oh, nothing.
I'm, uh, I'm just...

19:22.756 --> 19:24.356
here with my girlfriend
having a little, uh,

19:24.357 --> 19:26.525
a little birthday
celebration, you know.

19:26.526 --> 19:28.160
What are
you doing?!

19:28.161 --> 19:30.029
Oh, I'm sorry, I'm sorry,
I just, I love it

19:30.030 --> 19:31.730
when your hair is down--
it's so sexy. You know?

19:32.999 --> 19:35.501
He's right, it is.

19:35.502 --> 19:37.870
Would you like to
join us for a drink?

19:37.871 --> 19:39.305
Great idea!

19:40.123 --> 19:42.308
Uh, so, Lyndsey,
uh, happy birthday.

19:42.309 --> 19:44.126
Thank you.
Did you get anything special?

19:44.127 --> 19:46.512
LYNDSEY:
Well, as a matter of fact...

19:46.513 --> 19:49.515
All right, I just have
to say something here!

19:49.516 --> 19:51.984
You-you whine
and moan about

19:51.985 --> 19:54.220
not having enough money
to buy decent clothes

19:54.221 --> 19:56.589
for our son, and yet...
somehow there's enough

19:56.590 --> 19:59.992
for you go out and have a...
a big fancy dinner!

19:59.993 --> 20:01.026
What?

20:01.027 --> 20:02.061
Oh, oh, oh, oh,

20:02.062 --> 20:03.729
are you suddenly
hard of hearing?

20:03.730 --> 20:06.599
Or are you just...
allergic to the truth?!

20:06.600 --> 20:07.983
Oh, hey, hold on...

20:07.984 --> 20:09.935
No, no, no, no!
This needs to be said!

20:09.936 --> 20:11.937
You should be
ashamed of yourself!

20:11.938 --> 20:15.341
Shame! Shame, shame...

20:16.776 --> 20:19.161
Shame.

20:20.497 --> 20:23.448
Come on, Herb.
He's crazy.

20:23.449 --> 20:24.967
Happy birthday,
Lyndsey.

20:24.968 --> 20:26.468
I love the earrings.
JUDITH: Herb!

20:26.469 --> 20:28.137
Coming.

20:32.058 --> 20:35.060
Can you believe
I was married to that bitch?

20:35.061 --> 20:37.329
♪ Men... ♪

20:40.893 --> 20:43.083
(football game playing
at low volume)

20:43.183 --> 20:44.950
- Hey.
- Hey.

20:44.951 --> 20:46.418
Where have you been?

20:46.419 --> 20:49.354
Oh, I was, uh, dropping
Jake off at his mother's.

20:49.355 --> 20:50.956
How are you handling your guilt?

20:50.957 --> 20:53.258
Oh, you mean
about the earrings?

20:53.259 --> 20:55.728
Well, interesting thing.

20:55.729 --> 20:58.497
It's much easier
the second time.

20:58.498 --> 21:01.366
